<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Spring Symphony, Op. 44 (Benjamin Britten)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1949</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in (sung by a boys' choir at the climax)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Adventures of Robin Hood (film)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1938</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in (Little John whistles the melody)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Wicker Man (film)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1973</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as (a mixed translation by Anthony Shaffer sung at the climax)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ancient Music (Ezra Pound)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1916 (published 1917)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Summer is a cumin seed, in The Seasonings (P. D. Q. Bach / Peter Schickele)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Plumber is icumen in (A. Y. Campbell)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Mouse Organ Song (We Will Fix It), in Bagpuss</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody (tune adapted)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Mr and Mrs Smith and Mr Drake (album)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1984</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as (sung to a new melody)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">1000 Years of Popular Music (Richard Thompson)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2003</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as (his own arrangement)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Rant (The Futureheads)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2012</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as (a cappella)</span></li></ul></section>
